WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:07.980
Speaker 1: There are still endless gobs of
Republican elected officials who defend Trump.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.320
Marjorie Taylor GREENE.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.800
You know the folks.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:18.160
But there are more and more Republican elected
officials who are saying this is too much.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.710
Now, I don't say that these people are brave.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.230
Listen, the guy's been impeached twice.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.230
Humiliated.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:30.599
The country has been indicted twice, is admitting
to crimes in speeches made in front of his

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:32.029
supporters.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:35.079
These aren't brave people for doing this now.

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:38.239
But I care about the political ramifications.

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:40.070
Here is Ken Buck.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.809
Starting to go in the direction of this may
have been too much.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:48.460
Speaker 2: How would you have done it if you
were the prosecutor then after 14 months of

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:55.101
asking and then, of course, seeing the surveillance
tapes that showed even after a subpoena, they

00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:58.870
didn't get that the former president defied
a subpoena, according to this man.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.080
Speaker 5: And it goes beyond that.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.320
He hid documents, you know, purposely putting
him in a shower, purposely putting him on

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.320
a stage.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.610
So there clearly is an intent to hide or was
intent that he knew what he talked to.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:16.439
His attorneys so brief these documents that
no doubt that that it was a difficult situation.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:22.400
It's just the precedent from my position,
my my view of searching a former president's

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.659
home, that that is just unseemly in this country.

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:28.970
I don't know what the answer is, whether there
were alternatives or not.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:35.560
Speaker 2: I want to ask about the notion
of the former president being a candidate

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.610
for president.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.140
Again, as you said, he is innocent until proven
guilty.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.610
That is the way the system works and should
work.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.710
But given the allegations you just discussed,
some of them, the specifics of the way he

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:52.380
allegedly mishandled classified information,
would you feel comfortable with Donald Trump

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.430
as president again?

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.300
Speaker 5: Well, I would not feel comfortable
with a convicted felon in the White House.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.539
So what a big boy.

00:01:58.539 --> 00:01:59.880
Speaker 1: How brave.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.829
Now, understand, even for Ken Buck, like he's
still saying, a convicted felon, certainly

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:10.550
the allegations against Trump wouldn't influence
his vote, but he's at least drawing some line

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.500
in the sand as pathetic and weak.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:17.390
I mean, it it is a cop out, but it's also
pathetic that this is what it takes to get

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.930
them to even revise their thoughts.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:27.260
Then Mike Pompeo went on Fox News yesterday,
and he also is saying this is extraordinarily

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.260
serious.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.640
Speaker 5: With Donald Trump is facing and
is it right to charge him?

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.680
Brian, good morning.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.370
Great to be with you.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.140
Two things i think are both true at this point.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:42.540
First, if the allegations are true and there's
lots of indications that they are.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.110
President trump had classified documents where
he shouldn't have had them and then when given

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.159
the opportunity, return them.

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:49.470
Me, he chose not to do that for whatever reason.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.470
That's just.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.200
Brian, you talked about me having classified
documents.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.780
I handle thousands and thousands of them over
my time in Congress and then as a CIA director

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.340
and secretary of state.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.350
I suppose we can all make mistakes and get
into the wrong place.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.930
But when somebody identifies that, you've
got to turn them in.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.480
So that's just that's inconsistent with protecting
America's soldiers, sailors, airmen and Marines.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.190
And if the allegations are true, some of these
were pretty serious, important documents.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.980
Speaker 1: Now, the question for Mike Pompeo,
even though he's being big and tough now,

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.569
is you were secretary of state.

00:03:18.569 --> 00:03:23.500
Are you saying Trump never did anything wrong
until he left the Oval Office?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.650
Because that's becoming increasingly difficult
to believe from all of these folks who say,

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.610
listen, everything he did as president was
fine, but this one thing he did since leaving

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.570
that I'm not okay with, very difficult to
believe that former Speaker of the House Paul

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.270
Ryan was on with CBS.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.680
Now, he is not a Trump guy.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.250
We already know that.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:46.189
But he is also hammering Trump very hard from
another wing of Republicans that seem to be

00:03:46.189 --> 00:03:47.189
turning on him.

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:49.110
Speaker 5: And this one's national security.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.110
This one is different.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:54.150
I used to have these same documents myself
as speaker of the House.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.500
So I think this goes beyond just some petty
thing.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:04.299
Now, my guess is Trump will play this politically
pretty well and make this weaponization argument

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:06.410
and make this about Joe Biden's Justice Department.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.280
And that's going to have some political saliency.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.280
So I don't think Mark was wrong in saying
that there's some political sting here, But

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:18.199
I can't help but think the weight in the baggage
of all of this and this one's national security,

00:04:18.199 --> 00:04:22.870
this one, I think we want a nominee who's
not weighed down with so much baggage in order

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:23.870
to win this election.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:24.870
Speaker 1: All right.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.640
So Paul Ryan saying Trump is not the right
guy.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.970
Paul Ryan was saying that before this second
indictment.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.259
Anyway, Fox News senior political.

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:38.700
Analyst Brit HUME actually explains the entire
thing here on this second indictment.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:43.440
This is not an elected official, but Brit
HUME is sort of the epitome of just put your

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.590
finger to the wind and go wherever the Republicans
want you to go.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:52.470
He's making it clear that this could indeed
be a moment for many Republicans to back away

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.470
from Trump.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.470
Speaker 2: What are your thoughts this morning?

00:04:54.470 --> 00:05:00.009
Speaker 5: Well, I think that there are two
things can be true at the same time.

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:05.160
One of them being that there is indeed a two
tier system of justice in which people like

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.850
Hillary Clinton skate while Donald Trump is
indicted for wrong.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.830
Speaker 1: And no evidence of that at this
time.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.010
But okay, can you please continue?

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.120
Speaker 5: Or similar or similar events?

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:23.150
That does not mean, however, that the indictment
is not valid and serious and it's details

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.630
are pretty damning.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:30.770
And I think that some of these politicians
who are quickly in standing with Trump and

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:36.442
and seem not to have thoroughly read or understood
the indictment, may want to may want to back

00:05:36.442 --> 00:05:41.271
away a little bit and and and let this that
the details of this indictment sink in.

00:05:41.271 --> 00:05:45.009
And when they sink in with the public, there
may be a shift in sentiment on this.

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:46.590
Speaker 1: That is for sure.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.590
That is for sure.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.590
And we are seeing that.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.590
A couple more of these.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:54.700
CNN reporter Manu Raju spoke to Republican
Congressman Steve Womack and Republican Congressman

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.910
Tim Burchett and some others.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.780
And many of these are already backing away.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:07.289
Speaker 5: They have serious concerns about
anybody that has a reckless disregard for

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:08.700
the handling of classified documents.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.210
A military guy, he.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.430
Speaker 2: Allegedly had national security
information.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.020
Speaker 5: Very problematic is the reason
I'm not not defending it.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.240
Would you be okay with that of a convicted
felon as your nominee?

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.000
And I just have to read the conviction.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.000
But no.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.289
Honestly, on the surface, I wouldn't.

00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:23.440
That doesn't look good.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.870
Speaker 1: There you go.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.730
So a number of these Republicans now, I want
to be crystal clear with you guys.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:34.530
I am not presenting these to you as examples
of bravery or, you know, moral clarity or

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.530
any of it.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:43.910
It is simply a sign that this may be what
allows and I think allows really is the right

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:49.169
word, allows inside a Republican support for
Trump to publicly collapse.

00:06:49.169 --> 00:06:50.780
We're going to continue watching it.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.090
What just one more little note on this.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:57.320
Pence now also saying he can't defend the
allegations in the Trump indictment.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.650
Pence on the New York indictment was saying
political, all that stuff.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:06.650
Now, Pence, after seeing this new federal
indictment, even Pence is saying he can't

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.650
defend that.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.440
So this may be a change.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.190
Just imagine where we will be 7 to 10 days
from now.

